%description:
The breakpoint distance of the urban path loss formulas takes the antenna heights above an
effective environment height of 1 m or more (TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1 Note 1: h'UT = hUT - hE).
A UE antenna at 1 m has an effective height of zero, where the formula beyond the breakpoint
has no value; it gave -inf or NaN without a message. The first evaluation of such a link is an
error, which tolerateHeightViolation does not switch off.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.ue[*].cellularNic.antenna.mobility.offsetZ = 1m
**.nrChannelModel[*].tolerateHeightViolation = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
the path loss of the scenario URBAN_MACROCELL is defined only where both antennas are higher than 1 m
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
